course: dictionary
lesson: 9786
title: Reading the words above the stage
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A surtitle is a line of words shown on a screen above the stage at an opera or a play. It gives you the meaning of what the actors are singing or saying, especially when they use another language. «Theatres often show translated words on a screen called surtitles» tells you that the words on the screen are a translation, so they help the audience understand.
explain: Surtitles work like subtitles on a film, but they sit above the stage instead of along the bottom of the picture. When you see «with English surtitles» on a poster, it means the opera is sung in another language, and the English words will appear on the screen as the singers perform.
explain: You do not need to read every word on the screen to enjoy the show. Watch the actors, listen to the music, and glance up at the surtitles when you need the story. Use the context of the show, the people and what is happening on stage, to check that the surtitle makes sense.
fact: A surtitle is shown on a screen above the stage.
fact: Surtitles give a translation of what is sung or said in another language.
fact: Surtitles can also help people who cannot hear well, because they can read the words.
fact: Surtitles are like subtitles on a film, but they are above the stage.
exercise: What is a surtitle? | A microphone that the singers hold close to their mouths | A cheap ticket for young people | *Words shown on a screen above the stage that translate what is sung or said | The seats at the back of the theatre
exercise: An opera is sung in Italian, and the theatre shows English surtitles. Why? | So the lights in the theatre get brighter | So the singers can see the words they should remember | So the orchestra knows when to start playing | *So the audience can read what is being sung in English
exercise: Surtitles are like subtitles on a film, but where are they shown? | Behind the curtain | Under the seats | *Above the stage | On the tickets
test: A visitor who cannot hear well goes to a play. How might surtitles help her? | They play music so she can hear the story | They make the actors speak more loudly | *They show the words on a screen so she can read them | They tell her where to sit
test: Which phrase tells you the opera is sung in another language? | «a play where the story is sung» | *«with English surtitles» | «many opera houses sell cheap tickets» | «the orchestra plays loudly»
exam: In the poster «with English surtitles», what does surtitles mean? | A film shown in a cinema before the play starts | Tickets that are sold only in English | Actors who speak English on the stage | *Translated words shown on a screen above the stage
